  "title": "Simons' theorem for minimizing hypercones that are regular with multiplicity one off the vertex (Simon B.1–B.2)",
  "statement": "Simons' theorem for minimizing hypercones that are regular with multiplicity one off the vertex (Simon B.2).\nData: P, m ∈ ℕ with 2 ≤ m ≤ 6; C ∈ 𝒟_m(ℝ^P); A₀ ⊆ ℝ^P a linear subspace with dim A₀ = m + 1.\nHypotheses:\n- C is minimizing in ℝ^P and ∂C = 0;\n- C is a cone: η_{0,λ#}C = C for every λ > 0 (IsConeCurrent C);\n- spt C ⊆ A₀;\n- every y ∈ spt C ∖ {0} is a regular point of C (y ∈ regularSet C) with Θ^m(μ_C, y) = 1.\nConclusion: every θ with Θ^m(μ_C, 0) = θ satisfies θ ≤ 1.",
  "lean_statement": "∀ (P m : ℕ) (C : GeometricCurrentOn (univ : Set (Euclid P)) m) (A₀ : Submodule ℝ (Euclid P)), 2 ≤ m → m ≤ 6 → Module.finrank ℝ A₀ = m + 1 → IsMinimizingIn C univ → BoundaryVanishes C → IsConeCurrent C → C.support ⊆ (A₀ : Set (Euclid P)) → (∀ y ∈ C.support, y ≠ 0 → y ∈ regularSet C ∧ HasMassDensity C y 1) → ∀ θ : ℝ, HasMassDensity C 0 θ → θ ≤ 1",
